.\"
.\" THR_EXIT(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH THR_EXIT 2 "May 2024" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
thr_exit \- terminate the current thread
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/thr.h>
.PP
.BI "void thr_exit(int *" state ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR thr_exit ()
terminates the current thread.
If
.I state
is not NULL, the kernel will set the value at that location to 1 and perform a
.BR futex (2)
WAKE operation on it after the thread has finished using its stack.
This allows other threads to safely join the exiting thread and free its resources.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 431
Arguments:      state (on stack)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pthread_exit (3),
.BR thr_new (2),
.BR futex (2)
